  "cves": [
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-97381",
      "publishedDate": "2026-10-13T21:08:05.334Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-10-17T00:50:41.672Z",
      "description": "Legacy Update is a tool for activating and installing updates on legacy Windows PCs. Legacy Update 1.12.0 through 1.13.1 contains an origin validation error in the IsPermitted method of its ActiveX control. After successfully reading the hosting document's hostname, a hostname that is not on the permitted list falls through without setting E_ACCESSDENIED, causing IsPermitted to return S_OK. An attacker who induces a user to visit a malicious webpage in Internet Explorer can invoke the control to enumerate update and system information, install updates without consent, display dialogs, or restart the computer when a reboot is pending. This issue was fixed in Legacy Update 1.13.2.",
      "severity": 9.9,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：LegacyUpdate LegacyUpdate\n🔓 漏洞类型：CWE-346, CWE-393 (CWE-346, CWE-393)\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
      "references": [
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/LegacyUpdate/LegacyUpdate/security/advisories/GHSA-f4g7-4gmx-jfgf",
          "type": "reference"
        },
